# op-v6: op-v5 + a dedicated SELinux type for the RIL spoof properties.
#
# Everything op-v5 carries is inherited unchanged (baked property-driven RIL, /etc/passwd
# self-heal, Redmi Note 12 build.prop masking); this layer only edits the vendor sepolicy
# so persist.vendor.orchid.ril.* gets its own type, orchid_ril_prop.
#
# The point is the screen. Those properties otherwise fall through to vendor_default_prop,
# which platform policy lets only init/vendor_init set, so the Cell-tower operblock had to
# run `adb root` — and under a root adbd minicap does not start at all, so the device screen
# stream is dead for as long as the operblock is usable. With this type the shell domain may
# set them directly (`su 0 setprop`), adbd stays in shell mode, and the two stop conflicting.
#
# The rule set was validated offline with secilc 3.5 before baking: it compiles both with
# init's own flags (-m -M true -G -N -c 33) and with neverallow checking ENABLED. See the
# header of bake-sepolicy.py for the two attribute memberships that are required to keep it
# neverallow-clean, and why deleting precompiled_sepolicy is what makes the edit take effect.
#
# Cost: init now compiles the policy at boot with /system/bin/secilc instead of loading the
# precompiled blob. Rollback is the untouched orchid-emulator:op-v5 tag.
FROM orchid-emulator:op-v5
USER root

COPY bake-sepolicy.py /tmp/bake-sepolicy.py
RUN python3 /tmp/bake-sepolicy.py && \
    rm -f /tmp/bake-sepolicy.py

USER androidusr
